<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="50671" href="schedule/2016/spring/CMN/496/50671.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2016" href="schedule/2016.xml">2016</calendarYear><term id="120161" href="schedule/2016/spring.xml">Spring 2016</term><subject id="CMN" href="schedule/2016/spring/CMN.xml">Communication</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2016/spring/CMN/496.xml">Adv Topics in Communication</course></parents><sectionNumber>CBU</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Comm &amp; Health Inequalities</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Explores the role that communication plays as both a potential contributor to existing health inequalities and a means of helping to reduce them. The class will draw on (1) theories and research from communication, public health and related social science disciplines and (2) illustrative policy and media examples that address key topics, such as communication inequalities and social determinants of health. Reserve for Communication majors removed November 18 by 9:00am.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2016-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2016-05-04Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S10">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1064</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Bigman-Galimore" firstName="C">Bigman-Galimore, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>